config BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_COMPUTE_AMD
	bool "AMD GPU compute host contract (amdgpu + KFD + firmware + dri/kfd nodes)"
	default y if BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_GPU_AI_ALL
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE
	help
	  Establishes the HOST side of AMD GPU compute:

	    * amdgpu kernel driver         (enabled via the kernel fragment)
	    * KFD compute interface        (CONFIG_HSA_AMD -> /dev/kfd)
	    * Radeon/Instinct firmware     (from linux-firmware, amdgpu/*)
	    * /dev/dri/* + /dev/kfd nodes  (udev overlay)

	  It deliberately does NOT compile the ROCm/HIP user-space stack (rocBLAS,
	  hipBLAS, the HIP runtime, ROCr) into the base OS. ROCm is enormous and
	  does not build in Buildroot; more importantly it belongs in the add-on
	  container. Ollama's ROCm image (and vLLM's ROCm image) bundle the whole
	  runtime and talk to the kernel through the /dev/kfd + /dev/dri nodes this
	  contract guarantees. See NOTES.md.
